# The old staging menu's ANDROID symbol no longer exists in mainline 6.12, so
# this driver cannot depend on it.  The Android version fragments enable it
# explicitly; it stays off otherwise.
config LOG
	tristate "Android kernel logger"
	default n
	help
	  This is the Android kernel logger driver. It provides the /dev/logger
	  interface used by Android's logging system (liblog) for kernel-space
	  logging. This driver was removed from mainline Linux in 6.12 but is
	  still required for Android 4.x and earlier.

	  If you are building Android 4.x or earlier, say Y.